  "final_assessment_score": 30
}

{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates lotteries based on their outcomes, specifically prioritizing the maximum outcome (the highest possible reward). If the maximum outcomes are equal, it then considers the minimum outcome (the worst-case scenario). In this decision problem, Lottery A offers 6000 Euros with 0.1% probability and 0 Euros otherwise, while Lottery B offers 3000 Euros with 0.2% probability and 0 Euros otherwise. The maximum outcome of A (6000 Euros) is higher than that of B (3000 Euros). Therefore, according to the decision reason, A should be preferred because it has a more favorable maximum outcome. The information relevant to the decision reason is clearly present and directly comparable between the two lotteries.",
